BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 738 Td
(  2. Protected API routes resolve the authenticated user from the session cookie.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 725 Td
(  3. User-owned product records are read or written with that user identity in) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 712 Td
(  scope.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 699 Td
(  4. The check-in is evaluated, a capacity estimate and contributing factors are) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 686 Td
(  computed, and a candidate action is selected.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 673 Td
(  5. Starting/skipping, measuring, and helpfulness feedback update the loop record) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 660 Td
(  and recommendation history.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 647 Td
(  6. Insights and history read back the user's stored records.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 629 Td
(  The repository includes endpoints grouped around /health, /auth/*, /signals,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 616 Td
(  /checkins, /capacity/now, /loop/*, /insights, /privacy/*, and /demo/*. The API) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 603 Td
(  docs and route implementation are the source of truth for request schemas.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
0.03 0.32 0.28
54 585 Td
(How to explain the scoring) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 562 Td
(  Use a simple explanation first: "The score is an estimate of current capacity) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 549 Td
(  relative to recent patterns, not a medical measurement.") Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 531 Td
(  For a technical judge:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 513 Td
(  - The system uses recent personal history where enough observations exist and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 500 Td
(    falls back or blends with broader prior values where history is sparse.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 487 Td
(  - It uses robust statistics \(including a median and median absolute deviation\) to) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 474 Td
(    reduce the influence of unusual observations.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 461 Td
(  - Available signals are standardized, direction-adjusted where needed, weighted,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 448 Td
(    and combined into a bounded 0-100 estimate. A score near 50 is the reference) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 435 Td
(    point in this scoring scheme, not a population norm or clinical threshold.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 422 Td
(  - A drop may open a recommendation loop. Cooldowns and daily limits constrain) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 409 Td
(    repeated interventions.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 391 Td
(  Do not call this a clinically validated biomarker or say a score diagnoses a) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 378 Td
(  person's state.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
0.03 0.32 0.28
54 360 Td
(How to explain personalization) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 337 Td
(  "We keep lightweight success/failure evidence for actions and use Thompson) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 324 Td
(  sampling over Beta distributions to choose between actions with promising history) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 311 Td
(  and some exploration. It is a way to personalize recommendations from observed app) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 298 Td
(  feedback. Our current simulation is synthetic, so we still need real-user) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 285 Td
(  evaluation before making effectiveness claims.") Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 267 Td
(  The measurement compares the user's before and after self-report and estimates) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 254 Td
(  expected no-action drift from prior control-like windows. Some values fall back to) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 241 Td
(  a prior when there is little history. This is not a randomized controlled trial) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 228 Td
(  and does not establish that the action caused the change.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
0.03 0.32 0.28
54 210 Td
(6. Privacy, authentication, and data) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
54 185 Td
(  Be precise about where information currently lives:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 167 Td
(  - MongoDB is used for authentication accounts and sessions.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 154 Td
(  - SQLite is used by the API for product activity and recommendation records. In a) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 141 Td
(    deployed setup, that would be server-side storage with a persistent volume; it) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 128 Td
(    is not device-only storage.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 115 Td
(  - Passwords are stored as password hashes, not plaintext. Session cookies are) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 102 Td
(    HTTP-only; server-side session tokens are stored in hashed form.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 89 Td
(  - The privacy UI includes consent, export, and deletion-related controls. Explain) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 76 Td
(    what these do only after confirming the current deployed environment and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
0.10 0.12 0.16 rg
62 63 Td
(    retention behavior.) Tj
ET
